#
#       A named FIFO is streamed through the shell-owned script fd. Claiming
#       its initial fd 255 moves the live reader to 256. Unlike an anonymous
#       pipe, the FIFO remains reopenable by pathname after aliases are closed,
#       so a restricted child is refused. The first line proves ordinary
#       unconfined FIFO scripts still run.
